Those go into **text nodes**. Django escapes them, the browser displays `&lt;img ...&gt;` as the characters `<img ...>`. Nothing reads them back out and re-parses them.

The dangerous copy is the one that left the template, travelled through `dataset`, and entered `html:`.

That is the pattern: **escaped-in-template is not the same as safe-in-JavaScript.** Auto-escape answers “will this break the HTML document I am rendering?” It does not answer “will the next API I pass this to treat it as HTML again?”

