The wrapper used `html:` so the hardcoded `<strong>Admin</strong>` would render as bold, not as the characters `<strong>`.

The template mixed two kinds of content in one attribute:

- Trusted markup: `<strong>`, `Admin`, `Manager`
- Untrusted text: `{{ entry.user.get_display_name }}`

Once those share one string, SweetAlert cannot tell them apart. The whole string is HTML.

