## How to apply this the next time

When user text meets JS, pick the API by what it does:

- `textContent`, `createTextNode`, SweetAlert `text:` / `titleText:` → display
- `innerHTML`, `insertAdjacentHTML`, SweetAlert `html:` / `title`, Alpine `x-html` → parse

If you want bold “Admin” next to a name, build two nodes in JS: a `<strong>` you wrote, and a text node for the name. Do not join them into one HTML string.

A payload in the DB is only XSS when a sink parses it. The tests lock that contract: a name of `<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>` is stored, the staff list and menu detail render `&lt;img ...&gt;` in the attribute, and `confirm.js` must keep `text:` / `titleText:`.

