So “cancel” can mean: **paperwork reversed, stock left where submit put it.**

---

## Concrete example

Monday you transfer 10 kg rice Store → Kitchen A. Submit snapshots `target_warehouse = Kitchen A`. Kitchen A now has the rice. Store is down 10 kg.

Tuesday someone points the FOOD production unit at Kitchen B.

Wednesday you cancel the transfer.

Cancel looks up “current FOOD warehouse” → Kitchen B.

Two bad outcomes:

| Kitchen B state | What the code does | Result |
|---|---|---|
| No bin for rice | `continue`, then `CANCELLED` | Kitchen A still has 10 kg. Store still missing 10 kg. Document says the transfer never happened. |
| Has 10 kg from some other receipt | Takes rice from Kitchen B, puts it in Store | Kitchen A still has the original 10 kg. Kitchen B is short. Stock appeared in one place and vanished from another. |

The first case is silent loss of the reversal. The second case moves the wrong warehouse’s stock.

Same shape if Store is reassigned, or a bin row is deleted.

